-- ============================================================================
-- D2 ASSOCIATE DEEP SEED: Machine Learning on Well Data, beginner tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed, and the question rows from the
-- committed bank JSONs under tools/course-banks/mlcore/beginner.
--
-- What this tier owns: A MODEL AND ITS TEST. A model is a rule fitted to
-- data; features and a target; why test data must be unseen; a split by rows
-- against a split by whole wells, the seed, the sorted names and the shuffle;
-- scaling fitted on the training rows with the population standard deviation,
-- and min-max without clipping; least squares, its coefficients and their
-- units, the intercept, standard errors and residual degrees of freedom; RMSE,
-- MAE and R-squared about a named reference mean; residuals well by well; one
-- well held out end to end. Digest sections 1 to 10, and section 26.
--
-- THE TRAP THE TIER IS BUILT ON. A score means what its rows mean: a random-row
-- split tests wells the model has already seen, a scaler fitted on every row
-- has seen the test rows, and one held-out split is one draw of wells. The
-- Associate capstone grades six Associate quantities and grades no penalty, no
-- fold and no classifier.
-- ============================================================================

values ('mlcore', 'beginner', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-what-a-model-is","title":"What a Model Is","lesson_keys":["l01-a-rule-fitted-to-data","l02-features-and-a-target","l03-the-ekene-wells","l04-what-a-prediction-is","l05-the-refusals-by-name"]},{"key":"m02-data-the-model-has-not-seen","title":"Data the Model Has Not Seen","lesson_keys":["l01-why-test-data-must-be-unseen","l02-a-split-by-rows","l03-a-split-by-whole-wells","l04-the-seed-and-the-shuffle"]},{"key":"m03-scaling-on-the-training-rows","title":"Scaling on the Training Rows","lesson_keys":["l01-why-features-are-scaled","l02-the-population-standard-deviation","l03-fit-on-training-rows-only","l04-min-max-and-rows-outside-the-range"]},{"key":"m04-ordinary-least-squares","title":"Ordinary Least Squares","lesson_keys":["l01-least-squares-on-several-features","l02-reading-a-coefficient","l03-the-intercept","l04-standard-errors","l05-more-rows-than-coefficients"]},{"key":"m05-fit-metrics-and-residuals","title":"Fit Metrics and Residuals","lesson_keys":["l01-rmse-and-mae","l02-r-squared-on-a-test-set","l03-residuals-by-well","l04-training-score-and-test-score"]},{"key":"m06-one-well-held-out","title":"One Well Held Out, End to End","lesson_keys":["l01-the-whole-workflow","l02-a-well-the-model-never-saw","l03-writing-up-a-fit","l04-the-capstone-brief"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
